{
  "format": 1,
  "about": "What protocol 1's build_config (citar/worker/__main__.py) makes of each case: \"expect\", the WorkerConfig fields the Rust helper's settings must equal, or \"error\", its SystemExit message. {dir} is the case's directory: the home (CITAR_DATA_DIR) holding helper.json, and where the other files are. stdin is no terminal, so no first-run question is asked. A case \"migrated\" is a 0.1.5 helper.json, which must lend no CPU. A case marked \"fix\" is answered differently by the Rust helper on purpose (see \"fixes\"), its \"helper\" being the Rust answer. Recorded by python -m tests.test_helper_config_cases --record; 4-05 deletes the Python worker, and this file stays the record.",
  "fields": [
    "server_url",
    "token",
    "base_url",
    "provider",
    "api_key_env",
    "max_concurrent",
    "name",
    "quiet_hours",
    "models",
    "insecure",
    "collect_hardware",
    "hardware_file"
  ],
  "fixes": {},
